tatus="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AIZAWA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HASHIMOTO, MASAHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITOH, TAICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAOKA, YOSHITAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUMON, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIURA, MASAYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGAWA, KATSUTOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>RYOJI, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TATEKAWA, MASAICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMACHI, HIDENORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUJIMOTO, TAKAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A vibration transmitting plate (155) is disposed on one side, across a row (12A) of openings, of a control board (30) with the other side brought into contact with a toner roller (1). A vibration generator (60) is connected to one end of the vibration transmitting plate (155) and a vibration absorber (64) is disposed at the other end. A progressive wave is propagated in parallel with the row (12A) of openings and a standing wave is formed in a direction perpendicular to the row (12A).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon l'invention, une plaque de transmission de vibrations (155) est disposée sur un côté d'un pupitre de commande, à travers une rangée (12A) d'ouvertures, l'autre côté étant mis en contact avec un rouleau de toner (1). Un générateur de vibrations (60) est raccordé à une extrémité de la plaque de transmission de vibrations (155) et un absorbeur de vibrations (64) est disposé à l'autre côté. Une onde progressive est propagée parallèlement à la rangée (12A) d'ouvertures et une onde stationnaire est formée dans une direction perpendiculaire à la rangée (12A).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>